=   entry .Vacuiscible   the mixin on an element made from a container tag: `apply(children*)` adds its children
-     detail
+     detail

-         A `Tag.Container` applied to attributes alone, as `Div(style = t"color: red")`,
-         yields an `Html.Element & Html.Vacuiscible`, whose `apply` takes the children in a
-         second argument list: `Div(style = t"color: red")("hello")`. Each child must be `Html`
-         of the element's `Transport` — what the tag admits — or `Unset`, which is dropped. The
-         result is an element of the same topic and form.
-     entry #apply   the element with the given children, each checked against what the tag admits
-   entry .Transparent   the mixin on an element made from a transparent tag: its children decide its topic
+         `Tag.Container`, применённый только к атрибутам, как `Div(style = t"color: red")`, даёт
+         `Html.Element & Html.Vacuiscible`, чей `apply` принимает дочерние элементы во втором
+         списке аргументов: `Div(style = t"color: red")("hello")`. Каждый дочерний элемент
+         должен быть `Html` из `Transport` элемента — того, что допускает тег, — или `Unset`,
+         который отбрасывается. Результат — элемент той же темы и формы.
+     entry #apply   элемент с заданными дочерними элементами, каждый из которых проверяется на допустимость для тега
+   entry .Transparent   примесь элемента, созданного из прозрачного тега: его тему определяют дочерние элементы

=   entry .Transparent   the mixin on an element made from a transparent tag: its children decide its topic
-     detail
+     detail

-         A transparent element — `<a>`, `<ins>`, `<del>`, `<map>`, `<object>` and the like —
-         takes its content model from its parent, so `A(Li("x"))` cannot be placed in a `<div>`
-         where `<li>` could not. `Html.Transparent#apply` records the children's labels as the
-         result's `Topic`, so `A(Li("x"))` is an `Html.Element of "li"`, admitted
-         exactly where an `<li>` is.
-     entry #apply   the element with the given children, its topic becoming their labels
-   entry .name   the format's name, `HTML`, as `Parse.Error` reports it
